{
  "info": {
    "name": "Pipelinq API Tests",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Newman API tests for Pipelinq Nextcloud app"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "basic",
    "basic": [
      { "key": "username", "value": "{{username}}", "type": "string" },
      { "key": "password", "value": "{{password}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// EVERY REQUEST IN THIS COLLECTION STATES ITS OWN IDENTITY. NONE",
          "// INHERITS ONE.",
          "//",
          "// Newman keeps ONE cookie jar per host. Nextcloud hands out a session",
          "// cookie on the first request, and — MEASURED on NC 32.0.13, in both",
          "// directions, on a freshly installed instance — once that cookie is in",
          "// the jar, an explicit `Authorization: Basic` header for a DIFFERENT",
          "// user is ignored: the request runs as whoever the session belongs to.",
          "//",
          "//   jar present  + Basic <non-admin> -> /ocs/v2.php/cloud/user says 'admin'",
          "//   jar cleared  + Basic <non-admin> -> /ocs/v2.php/cloud/user says the non-admin",
          "//",
          "// That is not a theoretical hazard here. 'PUT /rapportage/sla — non-admin",
          "// → 403' carried a request-level basic-auth block naming variables that",
          "// nothing defined, so it authenticated nobody, fell through to the",
          "// admin session in the jar, and returned HTTP 200 — the test asserting",
          "// that a non-admin is REFUSED was, in fact, performing the admin write.",
          "//",
          "// ⚠️ Do not 'simplify' this away by trusting the per-request auth block.",
          "// Curl does NOT reproduce the failure (its jar never captures the NC",
          "// session cookie in the first place), so a curl-based check of this",
          "// behaviour reports the safe answer for the wrong reason.",
          "const jar = pm.cookies.jar();",
          "jar.clear(pm.variables.replaceIn('{{baseUrl}}'), function (err) {",
          "  if (err) { console.error('Could not clear the cookie jar: ' + err); }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "username", "value": "admin" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "admin" },
    {
      "key": "nonAdminUsername",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Supplied by tests/newman/ci-seed.sh via the generated ci.postman_environment.json. Deliberately EMPTY here rather than absent: an undefined Postman variable is sent as the literal '{{nonAdminUsername}}', which authenticates nobody and lets Nextcloud fall back to the cookie jar's admin session — the exact failure the 'Rapportage (Reporting)' identity check now catches."
    },
    {
      "key": "nonAdminPassword",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Supplied by tests/newman/ci-seed.sh. See nonAdminUsername."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Caller identity",
      "description": "Newman keeps ONE cookie jar per host, so 'who is this request from' is not a property of the request — it is a property of whatever authenticated last. Every folder below that asserts an authorization outcome first asks the server who it thinks is calling, and asserts the answer. This folder pins the admin end of that; 'Rapportage (Reporting)' pins the non-admin end.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /ocs/v2.php/cloud/user — the admin chain runs as {{username}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/ocs/v2.php/cloud/user?format=json",
            "header": [
              { "key": "OCS-APIRequest", "value": "true" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ]
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('The server reports the caller as {{username}}', function () {",
                  "  var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.ocs.data.id).to.eql(pm.variables.replaceIn('{{username}}'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('The caller is in the admin group', function () {",
                  "  var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.ocs.data.groups).to.include('admin');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
